Looking at this problem, I need to prove that area definiteness for $\mathbb{R}^2$ implies area definiteness for $\mathbb{R}^3$. Let me first check for answer leaks — the problem contains only an example ($a_{123}=a_{124}=a_{134}=1, a_{234}=-1$), no solution sketch or formalization. No leak detected.

Here is my proof.

